WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.000
<i>This is the story of a massive mystery</i>

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.810
<i>that shook the afterlife 
and living world alike.</i>

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.740
I'm back.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.740
I've withdrawn the bonus money for the

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.280
Mortal Census Bureau staff 
from the Afterworld Bank.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.680
Finally.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.150
It's been half a year.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.890
Thanks, Kain-kun.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.630
Okay, let's hand out the bonuses.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:34.720
What the hell?

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.550
It's getting bigger and bigger 
and bigger and bigger and whargh!

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.900
It's a party cracker!

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:48.480
<i>This is the first incident to be told 
through the ages: The Mysterious Party Cracker.</i>

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:22.990
M's Tragedy

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.130
The Mortal Census Bureau's 
bonus money got stolen?

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:30.050
Yup, and that filthy Shirushigami, Kain,

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:33.880
was in charge of transport, 
so he's in deep trouble.

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.660
That sounds terrible.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.820
They carry bonus money 
in the afterlife by foot?

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.520
That's so quaint.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.620
Why are you guys here?

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.040
Just chilling?

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:47.810
Whatever.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:52.360
So the general Shinigami have 
all received a notice as well.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:59.530
This is a photo of the stolen duralumin 
briefcase that had the money inside.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:08.250
Rokudou-kun, I've been wondering...

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.700
What's up with this duralumin case?

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:12.520
Dunno.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:16.880
It doesn't not not not look 
like it could be the same one.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.910
It was already here by the time I got back.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.550
Rokumon, is it not yours?

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:25.800
It's not yours, Rinne-sama?

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.550
What exactly is inside?

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.060
It's...

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.070
...money!

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:41.910
<i>This is the second incident: The Mysterious 
Appearance of the Mysterious Cash Pile.</i>

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:49.440
Rokudou-kun.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:52.500
<i>Having lived poor for a long time,</i>

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:57.970
<i>Rokudou Rinne falls ill at the 
sight of large sums of money.</i>

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.680
<i>Wh-What is this?</i>

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.010
<i>Why is there a ton of cash in my room?</i>

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.160
No!

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.980
I just can't look at it directly!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.730
Rokudou, you're...

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.360
I knew you were having a hard time, 
but I didn't know it was this bad.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.630
Wait, Jumonji!

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:29.110
Rinne wouldn't steal money just 
because he doesn't have money.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.470
Kain's so gross.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.690
I bet he did it just to piss you off.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:34.620
Pupupu.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:37.840
Ageha-sama, that's not nice, either.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:43.290
So, where should we hide this?

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:46.720
Or maybe we should take the 
whole thing and offshore it.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.950
What the hell are you all talking about?

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.150
I wouldn't—

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.930
I knew you took it!

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.450
You hobo Shinigami!

00:04:58.790 --> 00:04:59.800
Oh my, Kain.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.030
You're finally here.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.850
How could you call me guilty? That's slander.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.070
What evidence do you have?

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:05.840
Crunch.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.370
Explain this money.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.070
Rock-solid evidence.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:11.170
<i>This is a set-up.</i>

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:13.820
<i>Someone's trying to entrap me.</i>

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:28.770
Rokudou and the money vanished.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:33.740
<i>And then there was the third incident:</i>

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:38.350
<i>I call it The Mysterious Theft 
of the Mysterious Cash Pile.</i>

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:41.230
Damn you, Rokudou Rinne.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:47.110
I'll chase you to the depths of Hell and 
have your soul seized for a thousand years!

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:53.990
I hope Rinne-sama can get away.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.830
But I wonder if it was really 
Rokudou-kun that stole it.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.970
Mamiya-san, why would you say that now?

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:03.130
We just saw him take it and run.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.780
But it was a sloppy crime.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:10.140
I think Rokudou-kun would do a 
better job if he really wanted to.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:12.800
Now that you mention it...

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:16.230
That's true, it didn't have 
his usual skeevy touch.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.740
Where'd he go?

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:24.110
I'm sure he ran pretty far.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.830
That was a close one, huh, Rinne-kun?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:33.620
Masato.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:42.210
<i>Masato, written "ma" as in "demon," and 
"sato" as in a tight, narrow-minded person.</i>

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:47.130
<i>He's an anal retentive demon who holds 
several grudges against Rokudou Rinne.</i>

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.420
Ow!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.130
Is this your doing?

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.680
How rude. I helped you out.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.060
Why do I need to be escaping with you?

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:00.810
You were the one that stole the money from 
Kain and put it in my room, aren't you?

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.440
That's quite a false accusation.

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:08.990
In fact, you could say I'm a victim.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.200
Oh?

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:13.700
It happened this morning.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:17.450
Fireworks

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:21.450
I'm here for the party crackers I ordered.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.330
Here you are.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:24.660
Wait.

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:28.070
You're a demon. Why would you go 
shopping in an afterlife shop?

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:30.710
Why do you think?

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:34.090
The shops in Hell sell a lot of defects.

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:36.490
Even as a demon, I can't let my guard down.

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.360
That's the way Hell is.

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:42.850
That's why I make a point to shop 
at the more ethical afterlife shops.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:46.150
And right when I left the shop...

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:47.650
Look out!

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.360
A pegasus is on the loose!

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.360
On Sale! Duralumin cases
 For all your carrying needs

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.210
<i>What? A pegasus?</i>

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:57.300
<i>Holy hallucinations!</i>

00:07:57.980 --> 00:07:58.970
Oh?

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.210
I must have been out of 
it for about five minutes.

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:06.770
When I came to, the scene was cleaned up.

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:09.070
The duralumin case was safe, too.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:13.500
<i>That was awful.</i>

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.350
I was in a crappy mood, so...

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:29.220
I figured I'd leave you to 
discover the party crackers,

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.090
and laugh like a maniac at 
the sight of your squirming.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.490
Dude.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:43.120
kapapapapapow

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:43.120
Just like this.

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:44.670
Dude.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:48.290
But the crackers got swapped out!

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:49.280
Ow.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.440
Why'd you hit me?

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:56.430
So you were the one that left the 
duralumin case behind, weren't you?

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:00.720
Rokudou Rinne!

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:01.990
It's Kain.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:04.520
I doubt he'd be willing 
to listen in that state.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.940
Rinne-kun, Rinne-kun.

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:09.480
Handcuffs?!

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:15.780
I thought it'd be nice to see you panic, 
accused of a crime you didn't commit.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.530
Oh?

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:22.620
The cash robber's right here!

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:24.170
This is bad.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.100
Let's bounce, boss.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.250
Boss, you say?

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:30.750
You had an accomplice?

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:32.200
Let me go!

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.970
You're making it look like I'm an accomplice!

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:36.230
Exactly.

00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:38.010
I'm taking you to Hell with me.

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:49.980
<i>And so, suspect Rokudou Rinne, in his 
desperation, attempted an escape with Masato.</i>

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:58.110
Rokudou-kun's fleeing with a demon?

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.200
Is that true?

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.950
Yeah, they were definitely working together.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:07.010
He colluded with a demon to steal 
money from the Mortal Census Bureau.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:10.380
Rokudou's Shinigami life is all but over.

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:11.950
Demon?

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:13.930
I bet it's Masato.

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:18.990
I mean, it's kind of confusing 
when you say "Shinigami life,"

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:21.100
because I don't even know if they're 
dead or alive to begin with.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:21.890
Seriously?

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:36.120
So, Rinne-kun, what should we do?

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.450
A fancy dinner?

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.120
Game?

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:44.790
Shop?

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.110
Oh, a show?

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:49.760
We have plenty of money.

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:51.880
Let's use it all up.

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:54.630
Are you stupid?

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:58.140
Do you think I'd fall for 
such demon's whispers?

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:03.550
Rinne-kun, you say that, but it's 
already too late to turn back.

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:06.390
You can't convince them 
you're innocent anyway,

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.290
so let's just party up.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:10.140
Pah!

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:16.320
Masato, you <i>really</i> didn't 
steal this money, did you?

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.820
Like I said, I got caught up in an accident.

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:28.540
By the time I came to, someone had 
already swapped out the duralumin case.

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:36.690
What's the point of coming back 
to the scene of the accident?

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:38.380
What do you think?

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:44.930
I don't care for this, but Masato, I'm going 
to prove that you didn't steal this money.

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:46.120
Rinne-kun.

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:53.560
You really believe me?

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.550
Of course.

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:56.900
Whoopsie-daisy.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.030
Who're you?

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.910
The fireworks shop owner.

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:06.910
<i>The fireworks shop owner 
agreed to stand as a witness.</i>

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.930
<i>Let us begin the questioning.</i>

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:12.710
It happened this morning.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:16.710
I'm here for the party crackers I ordered.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.500
Here you are.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.630
Goodbye.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:26.140
Sir, I must have your payment.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.120
Payment, huh?

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.520
Will this do?

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:41.460
The pinwheel firecracker set off some other 
fireworks, and I suffered huge losses.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:46.490
Meanwhile, the demon got away.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.780
Staaaaaaaaaaaare.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:51.310
I don't remember that.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:53.710
Let's skip the silly lies, shall we?

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:58.950
You don't trust me?!

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:00.200
Of course I don't.

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:04.510
Fine. I'll pay for the damages.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:06.920
How much is it?

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:09.510
Don't use that.

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:14.560
But how did the duralumin case 
with the cash in it get stolen?

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.260
Carelessness.

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:17.750
You're so sloppy.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:19.000
No!

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:23.570
<i>Let's determine the truth 
based on Kain's testimony.</i>

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:26.110
Bank

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:29.310
I'm here to pick up the bonus money 
for the Mortal Census Bureau.

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:32.300
Yes, I have it right here.

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:34.360
Be safe on your way home.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:38.580
As I was walking back from the bank...

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:41.010
Duralumin cases!

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:43.880
High-quality duralumin cases!

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:45.690
On sale!

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:49.460
Two for one, limited time offer!

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:57.120
Fireworks

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:51.030
Duralumin cases, huh?

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:52.740
I don't need one.

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:56.910
And just then, there was a sudden explosion.

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:10.360
Yeah? So that actually happened?

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:12.710
I must have been passed out 
for three minutes or so.

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:15.160
And then? What happened next?

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:19.430
When I came to, there were 
duralumin cases everywhere.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:31.550
So the duralumin case got swapped 
out while you were unconscious?

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:34.810
And he was clever.

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:36.480
There.

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:39.050
This one.

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:41.560
M for Mortal Census Bureau.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.190
M.

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:47.410
I believe Rokudou Rinne prepared 
the same duralumin case

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:50.730
ahead of time before he 
stole the cash, and...

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.180
Neigh!

00:14:57.010 --> 00:14:58.070
The bonus money!

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:03.920
Sweet! I'll just leave 
this duralumin case here.

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:12.640
And just like that, he swapped 
it out while I was unconscious.

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:15.970
Who's that?

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.080
Dunno.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:20.100
It looks like Kain, 
but it's someone else, right?

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:24.190
Now you know how heinous a criminal he is.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.820
Who are you calling a heinous criminal?

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:28.570
Rokudou-kun.

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:30.630
I heard what you said.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.820
It was you, Kain, you did it.

00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:37.200
Me?

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.040
Crunch!

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:42.710
Look at you, acting so victorious 
as you hold a case full of cash.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.710
Listen to me!

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:48.090
I don't care to fall for your delay tactics.

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:53.100
Get him, Rinne-kun.

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.760
Get that damn Shirushigami.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.260
Rinne!

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.260
Rinne-sama!

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:06.230
How dare you!

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.230
Mrrrowrrr!

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.990
So you two were acting together.

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:14.200
You heinous criminal!

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.850
I told you, I'm not!

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:29.530
Wait, guys.

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:33.200
Mamiya-san, don't go near these 
violent people, it's dangerous.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:35.180
Let's go have tea or something.

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:38.850
Take this!

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:44.590
What was that for?!

00:16:44.590 --> 00:16:45.600
Holy Ash!

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:47.110
Holy Ash!

00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:48.860
Holy Ash!

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:54.650
Oy vey.

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:00.310
You want me to use this?

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:02.830
On the house, limited time special offer.

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:17.800
<i>And the answer to all of 
the mysteries was at hand.</i>

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:27.770
I'm not guilty.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:32.070
In fact, Kain, you were the one 
that caused this whole incident.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.290
What?

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:36.740
Look at the "M" on the duralumin case.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:37.780
The "M"?

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:40.910
There's a guy whose name 
starts with M right here.

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:44.980
I'm Demon Masato.

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:48.420
A man with a duralumin 
case marked with an "M".

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:49.670
What?

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:53.240
M is indeed my initial.

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:55.110
M as in akuMa.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.880
That's not what "initial" means.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.310
He's dumb.

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:08.350
Fireworks

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:06.150
<i>Let's look at everything chronologically.</i>

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:08.350
<i>Here are the facts:</i>

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:15.860
<i>The fireworks at the shop go off.</i>

00:18:19.310 --> 00:18:22.260
<i>The duralumin case carriage horse runs away.</i>

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:25.830
<i>It hits Kain.</i>

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:30.190
Holy Hand Grenade!

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:32.550
<i>And then it hits Masato.</i>

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:41.210
<i>And then as Kain came to soon after...</i>

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:52.520
Which means, Kain, you accidentally 
took Masato's duralumin case home.

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:54.980
Indeed.

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:59.360
Amidst the mountain of duralumin 
cases, you found the "M" mark,

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:02.950
and you didn't expect 
there to be more than one.

00:19:07.030 --> 00:19:14.860
<i>And Masato was left with another 
duralumin case with an "M" on it.</i>

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:22.980
Those are the facts!

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.350
So it's finally solved.

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:27.630
Kain!

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:29.340
Apologize to Rinne!

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:31.600
You accused him of a crime 
without even hearing him out.

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:35.950
<i>Bow down to Rokudou Rinne?</i>

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:38.120
<i>That's more shameful than even death.</i>

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:42.000
Exactly, you don't need to apologize.

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:47.870
There <i>was</i> a duralumin case in Rinne's room.

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.870
Just run!

00:19:50.740 --> 00:19:52.790
A demon's whisper!

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.540
You left it there.

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:56.950
How could you, Rinne-kun?

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:59.170
I did it for your sake.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.270
Lies.

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:04.540
You said you were in a crappy mood.

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:13.060
Well, technically, I did it because 
I wanted to see you squirm.

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:15.320
The money.

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:17.190
You're going to run off 
with it after all that?!

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:20.270
Run off with it?

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:23.460
Sadly, I'm not strapped for cash.

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:29.120
But as a token of gratitude for putting 
me through hell, I'll burn all the money!

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:34.080
Hellfire!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.250
Stop!

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:38.430
Oh, no. If the bonus money 
gets turned to ash...

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:39.840
What a scandal, huh?

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:42.840
Sic 'em, boy!

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:50.580
The duralumin case.

00:20:51.690 --> 00:20:53.640
I put a Yorishiro Sticker on it.

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:05.660
Yorishiro Sticker

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:02.080
A Yorishiro Sticker is a 
Shinigami tool that causes

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:05.660
whatever or whomever it's put 
on to be possessed by a spirit.

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:09.500
Aside from this dog spirit, 
there are also frogs, bears,

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:14.410
alligators, chickens, snakes, 
sharks, and all kinds of others.

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:26.070
With that said, I should have 
been a little more vigilant.

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:28.310
Sorry, you.

00:21:28.310 --> 00:21:29.860
I forgive you.

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:35.190
Rokudou Rinne.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:35.700
S—

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:36.610
Don't apologize, Kain.

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:38.940
It's not like you.

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:47.320
But I'm taking some out of your bonus 
to pay for the Yorishiro Sticker.

00:21:51.190 --> 00:21:52.850
You're so awesome, Rinne.

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:54.480
So generous.

00:21:55.030 --> 00:21:58.250
Let's call it even, then.

00:21:59.060 --> 00:21:59.750
Yeah.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:08.120
<i>And that's the story of The 
Mysterious Cash Robbery.</i>

00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:10.930
<i>Happily ever after.</i>

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:13.860
<i>He's a demon.</i>

00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:20.150
Click, click, click....

00:22:21.930 --> 00:22:25.400
Yorishiro Stickers are 10 yen each.

00:22:25.400 --> 00:22:27.610
I saw you take ten thousand yen.

00:22:28.170 --> 00:22:29.370
For my troubles.

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:25.980
Next Episode:
Merry Christmas in the Derelict

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:03.070
Ten thousand yen!

00:24:03.070 --> 00:24:04.700
Ten thousand yen!

00:24:04.700 --> 00:24:06.480
We did it, Rinne-sama.

00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:08.530
We wrangled good money out of Kain.

00:24:08.530 --> 00:24:09.730
All right, let's do this.

00:24:09.730 --> 00:24:10.800
Do what?

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:12.220
Christmas is coming up.

00:24:12.220 --> 00:24:14.200
I'm going to live it up with this money.

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:15.620
L-Live it up?!

00:24:15.620 --> 00:24:16.680
You?

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:17.720
Live it up?!

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:18.580
Yeah.

00:24:18.580 --> 00:24:21.560
I'm going to buy that thing 
I've always dreamed of having.

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:25.980
Next time on <i>Rin-ne</i>:
"Merry Christmas in the Derelict."
